---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site';
import styles from '@/styles/pages/listing.module.css';

const { email, github } = SITE.socials;
const contact = email ? `mailto:${email}` : github;
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects, why, and your rights.">
	<h1 class={styles.heading}>Privacy policy</h1>
	<p class={styles.sub}>Last updated 21 October 2026</p>
	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			This site is run by {SITE.author}, who is the data controller for it. For any privacy question
			or request, <a href={contact}>get in touch</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>What is collected</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Server logs.</strong> Like any web server, this one records each request: IP address,
			page requested, time, browser user agent and response status. These logs are used only to keep
			the site running and secure (legitimate interest, GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)) and are deleted
			regularly.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager, only if you accept.</strong> If you accept
			in the cookie banner, Google Analytics sets cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>)
			that count page views, rough location, device type and how you reached the site. This is
			based on your consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a)). Advertising features and Google signals are turned
			off, and nothing is used for ads. Google LLC processes this data and may transfer it to the
			US under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework. Analytics data is kept for up to 14 months. If you
			reject or do nothing, no Google script is loaded.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Comments.</strong> Post comments use <a href="https://giscus.app">giscus</a>, which
			stores comments in GitHub Discussions. Loading a post that has comments contacts giscus and
			GitHub. If you sign in to comment, GitHub's <a
				href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
				>privacy statement</a
			> applies to what you post.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Your browser.</strong> The site saves your theme and your cookie choice in your
			browser's local storage. They never leave your device. Fonts are served from this site, not
			from a third party.
		</p>

		<h2>Your choices</h2>
		<p>
			You can change or withdraw consent at any time with the <em>Cookies</em> link in the footer.
			Withdrawing deletes the Google Analytics cookies. Your choice is remembered for 6 months, after
			which you will be asked again. A <a href="https://globalprivacycontrol.org"
				>Global Privacy Control</a
			> signal from your browser counts as a refusal.
		</p>
		<p>No personal data is sold, or shared for cross-context behavioural advertising.</p>

		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR, UK GDPR, California's CCPA/CPRA, or
			India's DPDP Act), you can ask to access, correct, delete or export your personal data, object
			to or restrict its processing, and withdraw consent. You also have the right to complain to
			your local data protection authority. Requests are answered within one month.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>If this policy changes, the date at the top is updated.</p>
	</div>
</Base>
